  "term": "computerized assessment",
  "definition": "Computerized assessment is the use of a computer-based testing system to measure abilities or functions and score the results. In this source, it refers to a computerized working-memory test battery for young adults built from several tasks and a scoring norm to estimate overall working-memory capacity.",
